    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220-a1">

                <pb facs="0292" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg210"/>

                <head>Mr. Hitz to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate General of
                                Switzerland,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D. C.,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 31, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In compliance with the request of the
                    federal chancery of Switzerland, this consulate most respectfully transmits to
                    your honor the enclosed communication of the honorable federal council of
                    Switzerland, relative to the proposed introduction of the Swiss flag upon
                    vessels navigating the several oceans, and I would fain solicit a favorable
                    consideration of its contents.</p>
                <p>With assurances of high esteem, very obediently,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN HITZ, <hi rendition="#italic">Consul General of
                        Switzerland.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
